 "task": "Compute I = \u222b from 0 to 8 of f(x) dx on the PARCS cluster, where\n\n    f(x) = exp(-x / 4) * cos(x + 0.5 * sin(2 * x))\n\nFollow this layer plan exactly; it is part of the task:\n\n1. Split [0, 8] into N = 2 equal subintervals [a_k, b_k] with a_k = 8 * k / 2 and\n   b_k = 8 * (k + 1) / 2, for k = 0, 1, ..., 1.\n2. Run every subinterval as its own layer with parallelism 1: 2 subinterval layers in total.\n   Do not compute several subintervals in one layer.\n3. Each subinterval layer integrates f over its [a_k, b_k] with composite Simpson's rule using\n   10000 panels (accurate to about 1e-12).\n4. Then run one reduce layer with parallelism 1 whose previousLayerIds lists all 2 subinterval\n   layers. It adds up their results and outputs I. The reduce layer has 2 parents: read parent j\n   with input.GetPreviousOutputs(j) for j = 0, 1, ..., 1 (GetPreviousOutputs() alone reads\n   only the first parent).\n\nThe run uses exactly 3 layers. Report I from the reduce layer's output with at least\n12 significant digits. End your answer with a line of the form\n\nANSWER: <number>\n",
